884-// Flags that configure how the Builder behaves.
885-// The "Share" flags determine if the Builder automatically tries to pool
886-// this type. Pooling can reduce the size of serialized data if there are
887-// multiple maps of the same kind, at the expense of slightly slower
888-// serialization (the cost of lookups) and more memory use (std::set).
889-// By default this is on for keys, but off for strings.
890-// Turn keys off if you have e.g. only one map.
